{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGramBasisChange","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGramBasisChange","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGramProduct"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceGram_det_eq_sq_mul_prod_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceGram_det_eq_sq_mul_prod_matrix","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramBasisChange.lean#L137-L164","doc":"**The transport, composed: any Gram determinant of a Wedderburn-decomposable algebra is a\nsquare times the derived integer constant.**\n\nGiven a Wedderburn isomorphism `E` to a product of matrix algebras and *any* basis `c` of the\nalgebra, the Gram determinant of the regular trace form in `c` is\n\n    (det P)² · ∏ᵢ ± d_i^(d_i²)\n\nwhere `P` is the change of basis from the pulled-back matrix-unit basis to `c`.  The product\nis `regTraceGram_pi_matrix_det` from `RegTraceGramProduct`; the square is\n`bilin_toMatrix_det_basis_change`; the Wedderburn isomorphism itself contributes nothing, by\n`regTraceGram_toMatrix_map`.\n\nSpecialised to a Hecke algebra with `c = basisTwOfField`, the left side is `(twGram …).det`.\n**`det P` is not evaluated** — see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceGram_toMatrix_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceGram_toMatrix_map","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramBasisChange.lean#L113-L126","doc":"**Pulling a basis back along an algebra equivalence leaves the regular-trace Gram matrix\nliterally equal** — not merely congruent to it.\n\nThe regular trace form is an algebra invariant (`regTraceForm_algEquiv`), so transporting the\n*basis* along `e.symm` transports the form with it and the matrix of entries is unchanged.\nThis is why the Wedderburn isomorphism contributes **no** factor to the determinant: the only\nsquare in the whole transport comes from the change of basis *within* the algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isUnit_det_basis_toMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isUnit_det_basis_toMatrix","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramBasisChange.lean#L96-L103","doc":"**A change-of-basis determinant is a unit.**\n\n`b.toMatrix c` and `c.toMatrix b` are mutually inverse, so their determinants multiply to `1`.\nThis is what upgrades the square in `bilin_toMatrix_det_basis_change` from \"some factor\" to \"a\nfactor that cannot vanish\" — without it the transport says nothing about non-vanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.bilin_toMatrix_det_reindex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.bilin_toMatrix_det_reindex","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramBasisChange.lean#L81-L94","doc":"**Relabelling a basis leaves the Gram determinant alone.**\n\nReindexing permutes rows and columns by the *same* map, so the determinant is untouched — in\ncontrast to a genuine change of basis, which contributes the square above.  This is what makes\nit legitimate to compare a product basis indexed by `Σ λ, κ λ` with a `T_w` basis indexed by\npermutations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.bilin_toMatrix_det_basis_change","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.bilin_toMatrix_det_basis_change","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramBasisChange.lean#L68-L79","doc":"**A Gram determinant is basis-dependent exactly up to a square.**\n\n`BilinForm.toMatrix_mul_basis_toMatrix` gives the congruence `Pᵀ G P`; taking determinants\nturns the two copies of `P` into the square.  This is the reason a Gram determinant pins an\ninteger only up to `(det P)²`, and it holds for every bilinear form — no algebra structure and\nno trace is involved. ","signatureChunk":0}]}